A CI/CD pipeline is a series of automated steps that allow software development teams to frequently integrate code changes (CI – Continuous Integration) and deliver them quickly and reliably to production (CD – Continuous Delivery/Deployment). The pipeline ensures that every code change is automatically built, tested, and deployed, minimizing human error and speeding up the release cycle.

Why Is It Important for a Project?

Faster Development: Automates repetitive tasks, enabling rapid delivery of features and fixes.

Improved Code Quality: Early detection of bugs through automated testing.

Consistent Deployments: Reduces manual errors and ensures consistent environments.

Quick Feedback: Developers get instant feedback on their code changes.

Common CI/CD Tools

Version Control: Git, GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket

CI/CD Tools: GitHub Actions, GitLab CI/CD, Jenkins, CircleCI, Travis CI

Build Tools: Maven, Gradle, npm, Docker

Testing Frameworks: JUnit, Selenium, PyTest, Jest

Deployment Tools: Kubernetes, Docker Compose, Helm, AWS CodeDeploy
